💡 Button-Controlled LED Project

Project Description:
This project demonstrates a simple button-controlled LED using an STM32 microcontroller. It’s a beginner-friendly project that helps you understand GPIO input and output, digital reading, and basic microcontroller programming.

🔹 How It Works

A push button is connected to one GPIO pin of the STM32.

An LED is connected to another GPIO pin.

When the button is pressed, the microcontroller detects the HIGH/LOW signal and turns the LED ON.

When the button is released, the LED turns OFF.

🔹 Circuit Diagram
STM32 GPIO Pin ---- Push Button ---- GND
STM32 GPIO Pin ---- Resistor ---- LED ---- GND


