🔹 Code Logic (Simplified)
if (HAL_GPIO_ReadPin(BUTTON_GPIO_Port, BUTTON_Pin) == GPIO_PIN_SET) {
    HAL_GPIO_WritePin(LED_GPIO_Port, LED_Pin, GPIO_PIN_SET); // LED ON
} else {
    HAL_GPIO_WritePin(LED_GPIO_Port, LED_Pin, GPIO_PIN_RESET); // LED OFF
}


HAL_GPIO_ReadPin() reads the button state.

HAL_GPIO_WritePin() sets the LED ON or OFF.

🔹 Features

Learn GPIO input/output in STM32

Understand polling and conditional logic

Beginner-level project perfect for hands-on practice

🔹 Requirements

STM32 development board (e.g., STM32F103C8 “Blue Pill”)

Push button

LED and current-limiting resistor (220Ω)

STM32CubeIDE

🔹 How to Run

Connect the button and LED to the GPIO pins.

Open the project in STM32CubeIDE.

Build and flash the code to the board.

Press the button → LED turns ON

Release the button → LED turns OFF ✅
